WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:06.817
Water, earth,

00:06.901 --> 00:10.195
fire, air...

00:11.322 --> 00:15.367
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.451 --> 00:18.745
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.789 --> 00:23.709
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:23.793 --> 00:25.627
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.712 --> 00:27.004
he vanished.

00:27.422 --> 00:31.216
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.301 --> 00:32.884
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.969 --> 00:35.262
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.346 --> 00:38.015
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:38.975 --> 00:42.269
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:08.129 --> 01:10.589
Great. You're back. What's for dinner?

01:10.673 --> 01:12.090
We've got a few options.

01:12.175 --> 01:16.178
First, round nuts and some kind of
oval-shaped nuts.

01:16.262 --> 01:19.556
And some rock-shaped nuts
that might just be rocks.

01:21.893 --> 01:23.393
Dig in.

01:23.603 --> 01:26.063
Seriously, what else you got?

01:34.280 --> 01:35.989
What was that?

01:41.120 --> 01:43.789
It's coming from over there.

01:43.873 --> 01:47.834
Shouldn't we run away from
huge booms, not toward them?

01:57.595 --> 01:58.595
Hyah.

01:58.679 --> 02:00.222
An earthbender.

02:00.306 --> 02:01.473
Let's go meet him.

02:01.557 --> 02:04.017
He looks dangerous,
so we better approach cautiously.

02:04.227 --> 02:06.269
Hello there! I'm Katara.

02:06.479 --> 02:07.771
What's your name?

02:16.406 --> 02:17.989
Nice to meet you!

02:18.199 --> 02:19.866
I just wanted to say hi.

02:20.076 --> 02:22.327
Hey, that guy's
got to be running somewhere.

02:22.537 --> 02:23.954
Maybe we're near a village.

02:24.038 --> 02:26.373
And I bet that village has a market.

02:26.457 --> 02:28.458
Which means no nuts for dinner.

02:28.543 --> 02:30.627
Hey! I worked hard to get those nuts.

02:32.130 --> 02:33.505
Yeah, I hate them, too.

02:42.265 --> 02:43.473
Great hat.

02:43.558 --> 02:45.100
I'll trade you some nuts for it.

02:48.479 --> 02:49.855
Hey!

02:51.065 --> 02:52.190
Hi, Mom.

02:52.275 --> 02:53.483
Where have you been, Haru?

02:53.568 --> 02:54.568
You're late!

02:54.694 --> 02:56.403
Get started on your chores.

02:56.487 --> 02:58.280
Hey! You're that kid.

02:59.449 --> 03:00.490
Why did you run away before?

03:00.575 --> 03:03.368
You must have me confused
with some other kid.

03:03.786 --> 03:06.204
No, she doesn't.
We saw you earthbending.

03:08.416 --> 03:09.833
They saw you doing what?

03:10.042 --> 03:11.418
They're crazy, Mom.

03:11.502 --> 03:13.003
I mean, look at how they're dressed.

03:15.047 --> 03:17.340
You know how dangerous that is.

03:17.425 --> 03:20.635
You know what would happen
if they caught you earthbending.

03:20.720 --> 03:22.053
Open up!

03:25.057 --> 03:26.683
Fire Nation. Act natural.

03:36.277 --> 03:37.694
Aah!

03:38.279 --> 03:41.198
What do you want?
I've already paid you this week.

03:41.282 --> 03:42.866
The tax just doubled.

03:43.075 --> 03:45.202
We wouldn't want an accident,
would we?

03:45.953 --> 03:49.539
Fire is sometimes so hard to control.

03:57.673 --> 03:59.633
You can keep the copper ones.

04:04.222 --> 04:05.430
Nice guy.

04:05.515 --> 04:07.307
How long has
the Fire Nation been here?

04:07.600 --> 04:10.268
Five years. Fire Lord Ozai

04:10.353 --> 04:13.104
uses our town's coal mines
to fuel his ships.

04:13.314 --> 04:15.732
They're thugs. They steal from us.

04:15.816 --> 04:17.567
And everyone here
is too much of a coward

04:17.777 --> 04:18.902
to do anything about it.

04:18.986 --> 04:20.028
Quiet, Haru!

04:20.238 --> 04:21.571
Don't talk like that!

04:21.656 --> 04:23.031
But Haru's an earthbender.

04:23.115 --> 04:24.115
He can help.

04:24.325 --> 04:26.326
Earthbending is forbidden.

04:26.410 --> 04:28.662
It's caused nothing
but misery for this village.

04:28.871 --> 04:31.122
He must never use his abilities.

04:31.541 --> 04:32.791
How can you say that?

04:33.000 --> 04:34.584
Haru has a gift.

04:34.794 --> 04:36.211
Asking him not to earthbend

04:36.420 --> 04:38.588
is like asking me not to waterbend.

04:38.673 --> 04:39.965
It's a part of who we are.

04:40.174 --> 04:41.758
You don't understand.

04:41.968 --> 04:44.928
I understand that Haru can help
you fight back.

04:45.012 --> 04:46.513
What can the Fire Nation do to you

04:46.597 --> 04:48.014
that they haven't done already?

04:48.099 --> 04:50.642
They could take Haru away,

04:50.851 --> 04:52.561
like they took his father.

05:00.736 --> 05:02.571
My mom said
you can sleep here tonight.

05:02.905 --> 05:04.656
But you should leave in the morning.

05:04.740 --> 05:07.534
Thanks. I'll make sure
Appa doesn't eat all your hay.

05:13.457 --> 05:15.667
I'm sorry about
what I said earlier.

05:15.751 --> 05:17.210
I didn't know about your father.

05:17.295 --> 05:18.628
That's ok.

05:18.963 --> 05:22.257
It's funny. The way you were talking
back in the store,

05:22.341 --> 05:24.217
it reminded me of him.

05:24.302 --> 05:25.302
Thanks.

05:25.428 --> 05:27.012
My father was very courageous.

05:27.221 --> 05:28.972
When the Fire Nation invaded,

05:29.181 --> 05:31.600
he and the other earthbenders
were outnumbered ten to one.

05:31.809 --> 05:33.184
But they fought back anyway.

05:33.394 --> 05:35.186
He sounds like a great man.

05:36.105 --> 05:38.648
After the attack,
they rounded up my father

05:38.733 --> 05:40.400
and every other earthbender

05:40.484 --> 05:43.486
and took them away.
We haven't seen them since.

05:43.738 --> 05:45.655
So that's why
you hide your earthbending.

05:45.740 --> 05:46.740
Yeah.

05:47.742 --> 05:49.075
The problem is,

05:49.285 --> 05:52.662
the only way I can feel close
to my father now

05:52.747 --> 05:54.873
is when I practice my bending.

05:55.666 --> 05:57.917
He taught me everything I know.

05:59.837 --> 06:01.379
See this necklace?

06:01.589 --> 06:02.922
My mother gave it to me.

06:03.090 --> 06:04.299
It's beautiful.

06:04.383 --> 06:07.385
I lost my mother
in a Fire Nation raid.

06:07.470 --> 06:09.012
This necklace is all
I have left of her.

06:09.221 --> 06:11.222
It's not enough, is it?

06:11.307 --> 06:12.474
No.

06:17.730 --> 06:19.230
Aah! Help!

06:19.315 --> 06:20.315
The mine!

06:20.399 --> 06:22.108
Aah...

06:23.402 --> 06:24.861
Help me!

06:31.202 --> 06:32.786
It's not working.

06:32.995 --> 06:34.162
We have to get help.

06:34.246 --> 06:36.790
There's no time. Pull harder!

06:36.874 --> 06:39.459
Haru, there's a way you can help him.

06:39.543 --> 06:40.794
I can't.

06:40.920 --> 06:43.004
Please. There's no one around
to see you.

06:43.089 --> 06:44.464
It's the only way!

06:57.478 --> 06:58.728
Haru, you did it!

07:07.488 --> 07:09.864
It was so brave of Haru
to use his earthbending

07:09.949 --> 07:11.116
to help that old man.

07:11.659 --> 07:13.451
You must have really inspired him.

07:13.577 --> 07:14.577
I guess so.

07:14.787 --> 07:16.079
Everyone should get some sleep.

07:16.163 --> 07:17.247
We're leaving at dawn.

07:17.331 --> 07:19.290
Dawn? Can't we sleep in for once?

07:19.500 --> 07:20.792
Absolutely not!

07:20.876 --> 07:22.919
This village is crawling
with Fire Nation troops.

07:23.129 --> 07:24.754
If they discover you're here, Aang,

07:24.839 --> 07:26.339
we'll be eating fireballs
for breakfast.

07:26.549 --> 07:27.590
Good night.

07:28.008 --> 07:29.884
I'd rather eat fireballs than nuts.

07:29.969 --> 07:31.302
Good night.

07:55.119 --> 07:56.244
That's him!

07:56.328 --> 07:58.288
That's the earthbender!

07:58.372 --> 07:59.748
Aah!

08:28.152 --> 08:29.152
They took him!

08:29.361 --> 08:31.571
-They took Haru away!
-What?

08:31.655 --> 08:33.531
The old man turned him in
to the Fire Nation.

08:33.616 --> 08:35.909
It's all my fault.
I forced him into earthbending.

08:35.993 --> 08:38.578
Slow down, Katara.
When did this happen?

08:38.704 --> 08:41.456
Haru's mother said
they came for him at midnight.

08:41.540 --> 08:43.208
Then it's too late to track him.
He's long gone.

08:43.292 --> 08:44.667
We don't need to track him.

08:44.752 --> 08:47.253
The Fire Nation is going to
take me right to Haru.

08:47.630 --> 08:49.881
And why would they do that?

08:49.965 --> 08:53.176
Because they're going to arrest me
for earthbending.

08:56.263 --> 08:58.097
I thought you were
crazy at first, Katara,

08:58.182 --> 08:59.265
but this might work.

08:59.350 --> 09:01.476
There are ventilation shafts
throughout these mines.

09:01.560 --> 09:03.228
All Aang has to do is
send an air current

09:03.312 --> 09:05.146
from that vent to this one right here.

09:05.231 --> 09:07.565
The boulder levitates and ta-da...

09:07.650 --> 09:08.942
Fake earthbending.

09:09.026 --> 09:10.443
Aang, did you get all that?

09:10.528 --> 09:12.570
Sure, sure. I got it.

09:12.655 --> 09:14.155
Do you remember your cue?

09:14.240 --> 09:16.241
Yeah, yeah. Just relax.

09:16.325 --> 09:18.159
You're taking all the fun out of this.

09:18.244 --> 09:20.829
By "this" do you mean
intentionally being captured

09:20.913 --> 09:22.747
by an army of ruthless firebenders?

09:22.832 --> 09:25.291
Exactly. That's fun stuff.

09:25.668 --> 09:27.919
Here they come.
Get in your places.

09:30.631 --> 09:32.924
Get out of my way, pipsqueak.

09:33.008 --> 09:37.512
How dare you call me pipsqueak,
you giant-eared cretin?

09:37.596 --> 09:39.138
What did you call me?

09:39.223 --> 09:41.266
A giant-eared cretin.

09:41.350 --> 09:42.684
Look at those things.

09:42.768 --> 09:45.186
Do herds of animals
use them for shade?

09:45.271 --> 09:47.355
You better back off!

09:47.439 --> 09:48.606
Seriously, back off.

09:48.691 --> 09:50.483
I will not back off!

09:50.568 --> 09:52.068
I bet elephants get together

09:52.152 --> 09:55.029
and make fun of
how large your ears are.

09:55.114 --> 09:57.532
That's it! You're going down.

09:57.616 --> 09:59.868
I'll show you who's boss,

10:00.077 --> 10:02.453
earthbending style.

10:05.583 --> 10:09.168
I said, "earthbending style!"

10:13.007 --> 10:15.925
That lemur. He's earthbending.

10:17.845 --> 10:19.971
No, you idiot. It's the girl.

10:20.055 --> 10:22.432
Of course.

10:23.267 --> 10:24.893
I'll hold her!

10:25.269 --> 10:27.228
You've got 12 hours
to find Haru.

10:27.313 --> 10:29.188
We'll be right behind you.

10:37.031 --> 10:39.532
Momo, you have some big ears.

11:18.113 --> 11:21.574
She'll be fine, Aang.
Katara knows what she's doing.

11:28.874 --> 11:32.710
Earthbenders,
it is my pleasure to welcome you

11:32.795 --> 11:35.046
aboard my modest shipyard.

11:35.130 --> 11:37.548
I am your warden.

11:37.633 --> 11:40.969
I prefer to think of you
not as prisoners,

11:41.053 --> 11:43.346
but as honored guests.

11:43.430 --> 11:45.640
And I hope you come to think of me

11:45.724 --> 11:49.394
as your humble and caring host.

11:49.478 --> 11:52.605
You will succeed here
if you simply abide...

11:55.693 --> 11:56.859
Hyah!

11:58.570 --> 12:02.490
What kind of guest dishonors his host
by interrupting him?

12:02.574 --> 12:03.992
Take him below.

12:04.201 --> 12:08.037
One week in solitary
will improve his manners.

12:08.122 --> 12:11.666
Simply treat me with the courtesy
I give you

12:11.750 --> 12:15.336
and we'll get along famously.

12:15.504 --> 12:17.755
You will notice, earthbenders,

12:17.840 --> 12:21.259
that this rig is made
entirely of metal.

12:21.385 --> 12:25.304
You are miles away
from any rock or earth.

12:25.389 --> 12:28.474
So, if you have any illusions
about employing

12:28.559 --> 12:31.728
that brutish savagery
that passes for bending

12:31.812 --> 12:34.731
among you people, forget them.

12:35.482 --> 12:38.026
It is impossible.

12:39.069 --> 12:40.445
Good day.

13:05.846 --> 13:07.138
Katara?

13:07.222 --> 13:08.347
Haru!

13:08.432 --> 13:09.515
What are you doing here?

13:10.100 --> 13:11.976
It's my fault you were captured.

13:12.186 --> 13:13.644
I came to rescue you.

13:13.854 --> 13:15.646
So you got yourself arrested?

13:15.814 --> 13:17.690
It was the only way to find you.

13:17.775 --> 13:20.234
You've got guts, Katara.
I'll give you that.

13:20.444 --> 13:23.321
Come on. There's someone
I want you to meet.

13:24.782 --> 13:27.450
Katara, this is my father, Tyro.

13:28.285 --> 13:30.703
Dad, this is Katara.

13:30.788 --> 13:32.080
It's an honor to meet you.

13:33.957 --> 13:35.541
Have some dinner, Katara.

13:36.877 --> 13:37.877
Ew.

13:38.170 --> 13:40.046
It's not as bad as it looks.

13:42.508 --> 13:43.633
Eew!

13:43.717 --> 13:45.635
It's still pretty bad, though.

13:45.719 --> 13:47.345
Tyro, the prisoners are complaining

13:47.429 --> 13:49.263
there aren't enough blankets
to go around.

13:49.348 --> 13:50.932
I'll talk to the guards.

13:51.016 --> 13:53.976
In the meantime, make sure
the elderly are taken care of.

13:54.061 --> 13:56.729
The rest of us will simply have to
hope for warmer weather.

13:56.814 --> 13:58.231
If you don't mind me asking,

13:58.315 --> 13:59.524
what's your escape plan?

13:59.608 --> 14:00.608
Excuse me?

14:00.859 --> 14:03.319
You know, the plan
to get everyone off the rig?

14:03.403 --> 14:05.113
What is it? Mutiny, sabotage?

14:05.197 --> 14:08.324
The plan? The plan is to survive,

14:08.408 --> 14:10.952
wait out this war, hope that one day

14:11.036 --> 14:13.871
some of us can get back home
and forget this ever happened.

14:13.956 --> 14:15.832
How can you say that?

14:15.916 --> 14:17.416
You sound like
you've already given up.

14:17.626 --> 14:20.419
Katara, I admire your courage.

14:20.504 --> 14:22.588
And I envy your youth.

14:22.798 --> 14:25.216
But people's lives are at stake here.

14:25.425 --> 14:27.552
The warden is a ruthless man,

14:27.636 --> 14:29.971
and he won't stand for any rebellion.

14:30.222 --> 14:33.099
I'm sorry, but we're powerless.

14:33.600 --> 14:34.684
We'll see about that.

14:38.814 --> 14:40.523
Earthbenders!

14:40.607 --> 14:43.317
You don't know me, but I know of you.

14:43.402 --> 14:46.654
Every child in my water tribe village
was rocked to sleep

14:46.738 --> 14:49.073
with stories of the brave
Earth Kingdom

14:49.283 --> 14:52.201
and the courageous earthbenders
who guard its borders.

14:52.744 --> 14:54.787
Some of you may think
that the Fire Nation

14:54.872 --> 14:56.330
has made you powerless.

14:56.707 --> 14:59.584
Yes. They have taken away
your ability to bend.

14:59.668 --> 15:02.086
But they can't take away your courage.

15:02.171 --> 15:04.589
And it is your courage
they should truly fear,

15:04.673 --> 15:07.008
because it runs deeper than any mine

15:07.092 --> 15:08.551
you've been forced to dig,

15:08.635 --> 15:11.220
any ocean that keeps you
far from home.

15:11.305 --> 15:13.139
It is the strength of your hearts

15:13.223 --> 15:14.724
that make you who you are,

15:14.808 --> 15:18.186
hearts that will remain unbroken
when all rock and stone

15:18.270 --> 15:19.478
has eroded away.

15:19.688 --> 15:22.190
The time to fight back is now!

15:22.399 --> 15:25.484
I can tell you
the Avatar has returned!

15:25.569 --> 15:27.737
So remember your courage,
earthbenders!

15:27.821 --> 15:30.239
Let us fight for our freedom!

16:05.400 --> 16:06.400
Shh.

16:10.030 --> 16:11.822
Your 12 hours are up. Where is Haru?

16:11.907 --> 16:13.115
We've got to get out of here.

16:13.575 --> 16:15.034
I can't.

16:15.118 --> 16:17.536
We don't have much time.
There are guards everywhere.

16:17.621 --> 16:18.913
Get on!

16:19.122 --> 16:20.706
Katara, what's wrong?

16:20.958 --> 16:22.416
I'm not leaving.

16:23.752 --> 16:26.003
I'm not giving up on these people.

16:31.718 --> 16:33.344
What do you mean,
you're not leaving?

16:33.428 --> 16:35.513
We can't abandon these people.

16:35.597 --> 16:37.223
There has to be a way to help them.

16:37.307 --> 16:40.226
Maybe she's right.
What do you say, Sokka?

16:40.310 --> 16:41.894
I say you're both crazy.

16:43.814 --> 16:46.190
Last chance. We need to leave now.

16:46.525 --> 16:47.525
No.

16:48.110 --> 16:50.278
I hate when you get like this.

16:50.362 --> 16:51.737
Come on, we better hide.

16:53.782 --> 16:54.782
Go.

16:59.162 --> 17:00.413
Look!

17:01.164 --> 17:03.916
Tell me exactly what you saw.

17:04.001 --> 17:05.918
Well, sir, it looked like
a flying bison.

17:06.003 --> 17:07.003
What?

17:07.212 --> 17:09.005
It was a giant, flying buffalo, sir,

17:09.089 --> 17:10.131
with an empty saddle.

17:10.215 --> 17:13.175
Which was it, a buffalo or a bison?

17:13.260 --> 17:16.053
I'm not sure what the difference is,

17:16.138 --> 17:18.097
but that's not really the point,
is it, sir?

17:18.181 --> 17:21.225
I'll decide what the point is, fool!

17:21.310 --> 17:23.477
Aah!

17:24.938 --> 17:28.858
You! Wake up the captain!
Search the entire rig!

17:28.942 --> 17:30.234
-Sir.
-What?

17:30.319 --> 17:33.779
That was the captain
you just threw overboard, so...

17:33.864 --> 17:36.198
Then wake up someone
I haven't thrown overboard

17:36.283 --> 17:37.616
and search the rig.

17:37.701 --> 17:40.786
There's something going on here,
and I don't like it.

17:48.337 --> 17:51.255
We don't have much time.
What are we gonna do?

17:51.340 --> 17:53.174
I wish I knew how to make a hurricane.

17:54.676 --> 17:57.261
The warden would run away,
and we would steal his keys.

17:57.429 --> 17:59.680
Wouldn't he just
take his keys with him?

17:59.765 --> 18:01.849
I'm just tossing ideas around.

18:01.933 --> 18:03.100
I tried talking the earthbenders

18:03.185 --> 18:05.644
into fighting back,
but it didn't work.

18:05.729 --> 18:08.731
If there was just a way
to help them help themselves.

18:08.815 --> 18:12.318
For that they need some kind of
earth or some rock,

18:12.861 --> 18:14.320
something they can bend.

18:14.404 --> 18:16.113
But this entire place
is made of metal.

18:19.242 --> 18:21.118
No, it's not. Look at the smoke.

18:21.995 --> 18:24.038
I bet they're burning coal.

18:24.122 --> 18:25.498
In other words...

18:25.749 --> 18:27.041
Earth.

18:30.712 --> 18:33.381
It's almost dawn.
We're running out of time.

18:33.465 --> 18:34.965
You sure this is gonna work?

18:35.092 --> 18:36.175
It should.

18:36.259 --> 18:37.843
These vents reminded me
of our little trick

18:37.928 --> 18:39.095
back at the village.

18:39.179 --> 18:42.223
We're gonna do the same thing,
but on a much bigger scale.

18:42.307 --> 18:45.017
There's a huge deposit of coal
at the base of this island.

18:45.102 --> 18:46.811
And the whole system is ventilated.

18:46.895 --> 18:49.105
Aang closed off
all the vents except one.

18:49.189 --> 18:50.398
When he does his airbending,

18:50.482 --> 18:52.191
the coal only has one place to go...

18:52.275 --> 18:53.442
Right back here.

18:53.652 --> 18:55.277
There's the intruder!

18:55.487 --> 18:57.446
Stay back! I'm warning you!

18:57.656 --> 19:00.616
Katara, stop.
You can't win this fight.

19:03.286 --> 19:05.621
Listen to him well, child.

19:05.831 --> 19:07.706
You're one mistake away

19:07.791 --> 19:10.084
from dying where you stand.

19:30.689 --> 19:32.815
Here's your chance, earthbenders!

19:33.024 --> 19:35.484
Take it!
Your fate is in your own hands!

19:44.411 --> 19:45.828
Foolish girl.

19:46.037 --> 19:48.622
You thought a few inspirational words

19:48.832 --> 19:52.293
and some coal
would change these people?

19:52.377 --> 19:56.422
Look at these blank hopeless faces.

19:56.506 --> 19:59.508
Their spirits were broken
a long time ago.

19:59.718 --> 20:03.179
But you still believed in them.

20:03.263 --> 20:05.431
How sweet.

20:05.515 --> 20:09.101
They're a waste of your energy,
little girl.

20:09.186 --> 20:11.645
You failed.

20:15.609 --> 20:16.650
Grr.

20:18.695 --> 20:19.695
Hyah!

20:25.702 --> 20:27.244
Show no mercy!

20:30.165 --> 20:31.832
Aah!

20:31.917 --> 20:32.958
For the Earth Kingdom,

20:33.043 --> 20:34.418
attack!

21:10.038 --> 21:12.289
Get to the ship! We'll hold them off!

21:12.374 --> 21:14.166
Do not let them escape!

21:17.546 --> 21:19.296
Guys, throw me some coal!

21:33.270 --> 21:36.605
No, please. I can't swim.

21:36.690 --> 21:39.316
Don't worry. I hear cowards float.

21:49.953 --> 21:52.246
I want to thank you for saving me,

21:52.330 --> 21:53.622
for saving us.

21:53.832 --> 21:55.666
All it took was a little coal.

21:55.875 --> 21:58.168
It wasn't the coal, Katara.

21:58.253 --> 21:59.712
It was you.

21:59.921 --> 22:02.423
Thank you for helping me
find my courage,

22:02.507 --> 22:04.174
Katara of the water tribe.

22:04.384 --> 22:06.927
My family and everyone here

22:07.137 --> 22:08.887
owes you much.

22:09.097 --> 22:11.432
So, I guess you're going home now.

22:11.516 --> 22:14.059
Yes, to take back my village.

22:14.269 --> 22:16.478
To take back all of our villages!

22:16.688 --> 22:18.731
The Fire Nation will regret the day

22:18.815 --> 22:20.691
they set foot on our land!

22:21.985 --> 22:23.152
Come with us.

22:23.236 --> 22:24.361
I can't.

22:24.571 --> 22:26.322
Your mission
is to take back your home.

22:26.531 --> 22:30.075
Ours is to get Aang to the North Pole.

22:30.160 --> 22:32.202
That's him, isn't it? The Avatar.

22:34.998 --> 22:38.042
Katara, thank you for bringing
my father back to me.

22:38.126 --> 22:40.294
I never thought I'd see him again.

22:40.378 --> 22:42.046
I only wish there was some way...

22:42.255 --> 22:43.881
I know.

22:43.965 --> 22:46.467
My mother's necklace! It's gone!
